=====Usage notes=====
* The letter {{m|ru||э|tr=-}} is used word-initially and after vowels to represent {{IPAchar|/e/}} not preceded by {{IPAchar|/j/}}.
* It may also be used to show that the consonant preceding {{IPAchar|/e/}} is hard, but in the vast majority of cases the normal letter {{m|ru|е|tr=-}} is used instead. {{m|ru||Э|tr=-}} only occurs in the names of letters (see below), in the words {{l|ru|мэтр}}, {{l|ru|мэр}}, {{l|ru|пэр}}, {{l|ru|сэр}}, and otherwise when reflecting English {{IPAchar|/æ/}} as in {{l|ru|кэш}}, {{l|ru|рэп}}, {{l|ru|фэн}}. It is somewhat more common in transcribing foreign proper names.

